{% extends layout %}
{% block page_body %}
    {% set ph_kicker = 'Help' %}
    {% set ph_title = 'How CattoLMS works' %}
    {% set ph_lead = 'A practical guide to finding a course, getting access and learning at your own pace.' %}
    {% include '@platform/partials/page-head.html.twig' %}

    <section class="cl-page-section container cl-medium py-5">
        {% embed ui_template('layout.surface') with {props: ui_props('layout.surface', {section_spacing: true})} %}
            {% block surface_body %}
                <p class="lead">CattoLMS is a library of self-paced courses. You can browse the public catalogue without signing in, choose a course, and decide whether it is right for you before you buy access.</p>
                <p>Use the links below to jump to a topic. The information is kept visible on the page so it is easy to scan, print, search with your browser, and read with JavaScript disabled.</p>
                <nav aria-label="Help topics">
                    <p>
                        <a href="#find-a-course">Find a course</a> ·
                        <a href="#buy-access">Buy access</a> ·
                        <a href="#course-structure">Course structure</a> ·
                        <a href="#learn">Learn and track progress</a> ·
                        <a href="#sign-in">Sign in and your account</a>
                    </p>
                </nav>
            {% endblock %}
        {% endembed %}

        {% embed ui_template('layout.section-grid') with {props: ui_props('layout.section-grid', {columns: 2, section_spacing: true})} %}
            {% block body %}
                {% embed ui_template('layout.surface') with {props: ui_props('layout.surface', {id: 'find-a-course'})} %}
                    {% block surface_body %}
                        {% embed ui_template('layout.section-head') with {props: ui_props('layout.section-head', {eyebrow: '01', heading: 'Find a course', summary: 'Browse the catalogue and compare courses before you choose.'})} %}{% endembed %}
                        <p>Open <a href="/courses">Courses</a> to see the public catalogue. The first row shows the top-level categories. Select a category to open its related areas and subjects, then choose a subject to see the courses in that branch.</p>
                        <p>You can also search by keyword or browse <a href="/courses/tags">tags</a>. A course can appear under more than one tag, so tags are useful when you know the topic or outcome you want but not the category name.</p>
                        <p>Select a course card to read its description, estimated time, level, included material and available prices. The course page is where you decide whether to continue.</p>
                    {% endblock %}
                {% endembed %}

                {% embed ui_template('layout.surface') with {props: ui_props('layout.surface', {id: 'buy-access'})} %}
                    {% block surface_body %}
                        {% embed ui_template('layout.section-head') with {props: ui_props('layout.section-head', {eyebrow: '02', heading: 'Buy access', summary: 'Choose a price and complete checkout securely.'})} %}{% endembed %}
                        <ol>
                            <li>On a course page, choose the price and access period that suit you.</li>
                            <li>Select <strong>Buy now</strong> to go straight to checkout, or add the course to your cart if you want to continue browsing.</li>
                            <li>Review your course, price, access period and email address before placing the order.</li>
                            <li>Choose the payment method offered at checkout. Card payments in this environment show their result immediately; an EFT order displays payment instructions and an order reference.</li>
                        </ol>
                        <p>After a successful payment, your course appears in <strong>My Course Library</strong>. EFT access starts after the payment has been confirmed. Keep the order email and reference if you need to ask about a payment.</p>
                    {% endblock %}
                {% endembed %}

                {% embed ui_template('layout.surface') with {props: ui_props('layout.surface', {id: 'course-structure'})} %}
                    {% block surface_body %}
                        {% embed ui_template('layout.section-head') with {props: ui_props('layout.section-head', {eyebrow: '03', heading: 'What a course contains', summary: 'Courses are organised into a sequence of learning steps.'})} %}{% endembed %}
                        <p>A course is made up of modules. Each module contains the material for one part of the subject, such as written explanations, images, video, downloads or other practical resources.</p>
                        <p>Some modules finish with a module assessment. A course may also include a diagnostic at the beginning and a final assessment at the end. The course page explains which assessments are included and when they become available.</p>
                        <p>When a course offers a certificate, completing its required learning and assessments makes the certificate available according to the course rules.</p>
                    {% endblock %}
                {% endembed %}

                {% embed ui_template('layout.surface') with {props: ui_props('layout.surface', {id: 'learn'})} %}
                    {% block surface_body %}
                        {% embed ui_template('layout.section-head') with {props: ui_props('layout.section-head', {eyebrow: '04', heading: 'Learn and track progress', summary: 'Pause and return whenever you are ready.'})} %}{% endembed %}
                        <p>Open a purchased course from <strong>My Course Library</strong> and select <strong>Start</strong> or <strong>Continue</strong>. Work through the modules in order unless the course says that another path is available.</p>
                        <p>Your completed material and assessment results are saved as you go. You can leave and return later; the library shows your current progress and completed courses.</p>
                        <p>Read each module's instructions before starting an assessment. Submit your answers when you are ready and follow the result page for the next available step.</p>
                    {% endblock %}
                {% endembed %}

                {% embed ui_template('layout.surface') with {props: ui_props('layout.surface', {id: 'sign-in'})} %}
                    {% block surface_body %}
                        {% embed ui_template('layout.section-head') with {props: ui_props('layout.section-head', {eyebrow: '05', heading: 'Sign in and your account', summary: 'Access your courses without a password.'})} %}{% endembed %}
                        <p>CattoLMS uses a one-time sign-in link. Enter your email address on the <a href="/login">sign-in page</a>; the latest email contains the link for that sign-in attempt. A link expires and can only be used once.</p>
                        <p>Once signed in, your account area contains your course library, profile details, email addresses and active sessions. Keep your email address current so you can receive sign-in links and order messages.</p>
                    {% endblock %}
                {% endembed %}

                {% embed ui_template('layout.surface') with {props: ui_props('layout.surface', {id: 'answers'})} %}
                    {% block surface_body %}
                        {% embed ui_template('layout.section-head') with {props: ui_props('layout.section-head', {eyebrow: '06', heading: 'Still need an answer?', summary: 'We can help with questions about courses or access.'})} %}{% endembed %}
                        <p>Read the course description and checkout review first; they contain the specific access period, included material and payment details for that course.</p>
                        <p>If something is unclear or an order does not look right, <a href="/contact">contact the CattoLMS team</a> and include the email address on the account and your order reference where applicable.</p>
                    {% endblock %}
                {% endembed %}
            {% endblock %}
        {% endembed %}
    </section>
{% endblock %}
